(2870261, 398616, 25742, '<td valign="top">good composition<br/>this is obviously a photogenic spot and, as you say, you will not be the first or last to shoot this. Even the <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denali" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">wikipedia</a> article on Denali uses the same viewpoint</td>', 'good compositionthis is obviously a photogenic spot and, as you say, you will not be the first or last to shoot this. Even the wikipedia article on Denali uses the same viewpoint', '2006-09-27 19:41:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2870409, 398061, 51538, '<td valign="top">Train tracks are, IMO, impossible to avoid photographing.  They have a very strong symbolism - they lead somewhere - perhaps into the past, the future, or to another place.  They seem endless.  Old factory chimneys are also great symbols of a, mostly, extinct manufacturing industry.  Of blue collar work and pollution.  Your image has both in it.  I think perhaps rendition in b/w or duotone would have given this some age.  Probably worth another visit to the location.  I voted but came back to comment later....</td>', 'Train tracks are, IMO, impossible to avoid photographing.  They have a very strong symbolism - they lead somewhere - perhaps into the past, the future, or to another place.  They seem endless.  Old factory chimneys are also great symbols of a, mostly, extinct manufacturing industry.  Of blue collar work and pollution.  Your image has both in it.  I think perhaps rendition in b/w or duotone would have given this some age.  Probably worth another visit to the location.  I voted but came back to comment later....', '2006-09-27 20:47:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2870412, 395948, 21606, '<td valign="top">I think the signs are the important part here. They are the things you follow with your eyes. <br/> <br/>If I would have voted for this I would have given you a 7.</td>', 'I think the signs are the important part here. They are the things you follow with your eyes.  If I would have voted for this I would have given you a 7.', '2006-09-27 20:48:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2870469, 397942, 30982, '<td valign="top">I noted a comment about needing rotation - I disagree.  It''s lined up quite well, imo.  Has a definitely desolation about it.  Great perspective with the water in the foreground and I really like the way it "fades to gray" as it moves out.  Well done and underappreciated.</td>', 'I noted a comment about needing rotation - I disagree.  It''s lined up quite well, imo.  Has a definitely desolation about it.  Great perspective with the water in the foreground and I really like the way it "fades to gray" as it moves out.  Well done and underappreciated.', '2006-09-27 21:12:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2870611, 396553, 61191, '<td valign="top">I like your entry. Can''t explain why it didn''t do so well. Perhaps the leading line wasn''t leading enough ;) I guess people wanted to see a line leading to the central element which is your daughter (this is your daugher, isn''t it?). When you look at the shot, what do you see at first? The eyes. I think you should see the line at first which leads to her face and her eyes. Thus a composition with the "blow thing" rolled out and directed straight into the viewers face may have scored better. But this are all assumptions. I don''t really know.<br/> <br/>I love your creativity. Keep it up! :)</td>', 'I like your entry. Can''t explain why it didn''t do so well. Perhaps the leading line wasn''t leading enough ;) I guess people wanted to see a line leading to the central element which is your daughter (this is your daugher, isn''t it?). When you look at the shot, what do you see at first? The eyes. I think you should see the line at first which leads to her face and her eyes. Thus a composition with the "blow thing" rolled out and directed straight into the viewers face may have scored better. But this are all assumptions. I don''t really know. I love your creativity. Keep it up! :)', '2006-09-27 21:52:26.000000', NULL, 0),
