(2885193, 396741, 33560, '<td valign="top">I love how well it represents the way cities look and feel in so many parts of the US - an accretion of detritus built up over two centuries with virtually no attention paid to the overall architectural effect.  I also love the color pallet.</td>', 'I love how well it represents the way cities look and feel in so many parts of the US - an accretion of detritus built up over two centuries with virtually no attention paid to the overall architectural effect.  I also love the color pallet.', '2006-10-02 00:32:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2885642, 398265, 3936, '<td valign="top">Interesting picture....<br/> <br/>Although the ISO is 50, the picture looks a little grainy to my eye.<br/> <br/>I like the fog, and the half hidden shapes.  I agree with the other suggestions that the picture should be cropped right at the top of the column so that it does appear to go on for infinity.<br/> <br/>I would also suggest a slight rotation so that the column appears to be vertical.  With this view it appears to be leaning and could topple over.<br/> <br/>I like this picture and find it thought provoking.</td>', 'Interesting picture.... Although the ISO is 50, the picture looks a little grainy to my eye. I like the fog, and the half hidden shapes.  I agree with the other suggestions that the picture should be cropped right at the top of the column so that it does appear to go on for infinity. I would also suggest a slight rotation so that the column appears to be vertical.  With this view it appears to be leaning and could topple over. I like this picture and find it thought provoking.', '2006-10-02 01:54:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2885702, 396136, 3936, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo!<br/> <br/>Color, saturation, hue, brightness, contrast are all done quite well.<br/> <br/>Lighting is great!<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field are very good.  A little deeper depth of field would have worked well too.<br/> <br/>I have to agree with one of the other commenters, a little human interaction, (hand taking a bottle) would have been a nice addition, or even one bottle missing from the row.  Inidcating that someone is having a drink.  Would have been a nice touch.<br/> <br/>This is an excellent photo, and well deserving of a top ten finish.</td>', 'Excellent photo! Color, saturation, hue, brightness, contrast are all done quite well. Lighting is great! Focus and depth of field are very good.  A little deeper depth of field would have worked well too. I have to agree with one of the other commenters, a little human interaction, (hand taking a bottle) would have been a nice addition, or even one bottle missing from the row.  Inidcating that someone is having a drink.  Would have been a nice touch. This is an excellent photo, and well deserving of a top ten finish.', '2006-10-02 02:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2885737, 398075, 61373, '<td valign="top">wow did u use shadow highlights in CS? i like the composition in this pic very much. great detail. but the glow effect on the bridge is a bit much to me. in my opinion. keep it up dude.</td>', 'wow did u use shadow highlights in CS? i like the composition in this pic very much. great detail. but the glow effect on the bridge is a bit much to me. in my opinion. keep it up dude.', '2006-10-02 02:15:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2885743, 396986, 61373, '<td valign="top">awesome pic</td>', 'awesome pic', '2006-10-02 02:17:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2886515, 396986, 5354, '<td valign="top">Hey Hugh, good to see you back in the challenges. We haven''t seen too much of you recently.<br/> <br/>Beautiful image, those tones are so muted and delicate. Not the usual DPC fare, but worthy red ribbon winner. Congratulations.<br/> <br/>Keith</td>', 'Hey Hugh, good to see you back in the challenges. We haven''t seen too much of you recently. Beautiful image, those tones are so muted and delicate. Not the usual DPC fare, but worthy red ribbon winner. Congratulations. Keith', '2006-10-02 09:31:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2887225, 398502, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>The first thing I noticed was the two large white bands.  They really steal the impact of this shot by drawing your attention away from the boy.  I believe this was the fatal flaw to this photo and the reason it scored so low.  Cropping the white out would have helped the composition of this shot a lot.<br/> <br/>You had great timing on capturing this shot.  You were able to capture this before he realized that he was staring at a camera and a look of surprise took over.  I can just imagine that half a second later, he was gone!<br/> <br/>I see from your profile that this is your first entry.  Welcome To DPC!!!  This is a great site to really learn about photography and watch your own experience grow!</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  The first thing I noticed was the two large white bands.  They really steal the impact of this shot by drawing your attention away from the boy.  I believe this was the fatal flaw to this photo and the reason it scored so low.  Cropping the white out would have helped the composition of this shot a lot. You had great timing on capturing this shot.  You were able to capture this before he realized that he was staring at a camera and a look of surprise took over.  I can just imagine that half a second later, he was gone! I see from your profile that this is your first entry.  Welcome To DPC!!!  This is a great site to really learn about photography and watch your own experience grow!', '2006-10-02 13:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2887660, 396640, 60370, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your personal best.  I do agree with the crop at the junction point as well.  It would be a kick ass optical illusion if you did!<br/>You''ve come a long way since Frosty''s Little Brother ;-)<br/></td>', 'Congrats on your personal best.  I do agree with the crop at the junction point as well.  It would be a kick ass optical illusion if you did!You''ve come a long way since Frosty''s Little Brother ;-)', '2006-10-02 15:30:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2888389, 396136, 57202, '<td valign="top">AWESOME shot! :)  Personally, I think this should have ribboned.</td>', 'AWESOME shot! :)  Personally, I think this should have ribboned.', '2006-10-02 18:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2888416, 396778, 48389, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>I love the placement of the balloon in the frame, really draws the viewer to the great colours and lines. I may have been tempted to have the balloon completely filling the frame in the top right hand corner but other than that the lines from the bottom lead you right up to the tip of the balloon, I think this is spot on!<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/> <br/>The light is nice in this shot, your exposure is great but I do agree with one of your commenters, this could possibly do with a little sharpening.<br/> <br/>I am not sure that I can really do a lot of ''critiquing'' here as I feel the shot is technically good and composition is very nice.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>- Natalya :o)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Composition:  I love the placement of the balloon in the frame, really draws the viewer to the great colours and lines. I may have been tempted to have the balloon completely filling the frame in the top right hand corner but other than that the lines from the bottom lead you right up to the tip of the balloon, I think this is spot on! Technicals:  The light is nice in this shot, your exposure is great but I do agree with one of your commenters, this could possibly do with a little sharpening. I am not sure that I can really do a lot of ''critiquing'' here as I feel the shot is technically good and composition is very nice. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. - Natalya :o)', '2006-10-02 18:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2888420, 398171, 55956, '<td valign="top">*Greeting from critique Club*<br/> <br/>Hi, the composition is good and the choice of the black and white effect is perfect. where are the problems for this image and why it isn''t in a better position? I think for two reason. The first is that you lose details on the object, there is a bit of over exposition on it perhaps for the black and white convertion. the second is that the subject is too common there are much shots with this subject.<br/> <br/>Best regards and good luck for the next contest.<br/> <br/>gennaro</td>', '*Greeting from critique Club* Hi, the composition is good and the choice of the black and white effect is perfect. where are the problems for this image and why it isn''t in a better position? I think for two reason. The first is that you lose details on the object, there is a bit of over exposition on it perhaps for the black and white convertion. the second is that the subject is too common there are much shots with this subject. Best regards and good luck for the next contest. gennaro', '2006-10-02 18:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2888455, 397739, 55956, '<td valign="top">*Greeting from Critique club*<br/> <br/>Hi, your final score is the same of my rating during the voting. I think that there is a good black and white and a good angle. I loven''t these subjects (but this isn''t important). The only problem of the shot can be the out of focus in lower left side that is the start of the line.<br/> <br/>Best regards and good luck in  the next contest.<br/> <br/>Gennaro</td>', '*Greeting from Critique club* Hi, your final score is the same of my rating during the voting. I think that there is a good black and white and a good angle. I loven''t these subjects (but this isn''t important). The only problem of the shot can be the out of focus in lower left side that is the start of the line. Best regards and good luck in  the next contest. Gennaro', '2006-10-02 18:51:42.000000', NULL, 0),
